INSERT INTO listings (id, site_id, slug, name, description, website, content, entity_type, priority, is_unofficial, is_featured, is_active, status, published_at, display_order, source_kind, source_identity, source_updated_at, checksum, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('lst_2d4a2a09419685b9e843ed51', 'pornvideodownloaders.com', 'dreamcam-vr-downloader', 'DreamCamVR Video Downloader', 'VR content is massive and impossible to re-stream reliably. Save DreamCamVR shows to your device for flawless offline playback.', 'https://serp.ly/dreamcam-vr-video-downloader', '## Overview

VR content from DreamCamVR is large, bandwidth-intensive, and painful to re-stream. Buffering destroys the immersive experience, and live shows disappear permanently the moment they end. DreamCamVR Downloader lets you save VR content directly to your device for smooth, buffer-free playback whenever you want.

Record live VR streams with start/stop controls or download available VR recordings as MP4 files. The extension parses DreamCam''s HLS manifests and APIs to present available resolutions, then handles the conversion to MP4 right in your browser. VR-specific metadata like stereo packing, frame format, and viewing angles is preserved so compatible headsets can use the correct playback settings automatically.

Completed VR files are saved to a dedicated DreamCamVR folder. The entire pipeline runs locally on your device with nothing uploaded externally. 3 free downloads let you evaluate the workflow before subscribing.

## Why It Exists

- Save large VR streams locally so they play back smoothly without buffering or re-streaming.
- Capture live DreamCamVR shows before they end and disappear permanently.
- Preserve VR metadata so headsets use the correct stereo and viewing settings automatically.
- Process everything locally in your browser with zero external server involvement.

## Key Features

- Live VR stream capture with start/stop controls and elapsed-time tracking
- VR recording downloads with quality selection and automatic MP4 conversion
- HLS manifest parsing and DreamCam API integration for comprehensive quality detection
- VR metadata preservation for stereo packing, frame format, and viewing-angle details
- In-page download button on the DreamCamVR player for immediate access
- Quality selector with available HLS renditions sorted by resolution
- Built-in download manager with progress tracking, segment counts, and cancel controls
- Right-click context menu for faster capture starts
- Auto-saves finished VR files into a dedicated DreamCamVR folder inside Downloads
- Cross-browser support for Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Brave, Opera, Whale, and Yandex on desktop

## How It Works

- Install the extension: Set up DreamCamVR Downloader in your browser and verify your email through the secure OTP process.
- Open a VR stream or recording: Navigate to a public live VR performer page for capture or a VR recording page for downloads.
- Select quality and begin: Use the in-player button, popup, or right-click menu to pick your preferred resolution.
- Save the finished VR MP4: Monitor progress through the download manager and find the completed file in your DreamCamVR folder.

## Reviews

- VR files play perfectly (5/5): The stereo metadata carries over correctly so my headset reads the settings immediately. No more manual configuration. - Taylor Reeves
- Buffer-free VR at last (4.9/5): Re-streaming VR was always laggy. Now I just save the file and playback is flawless every time. - Chris Tanaka
- Reliable local processing (4.8/5): Everything processes in the browser. Large VR files complete without errors and land in the right folder. - Morgan Bailey

## Platform Support

### Browsers

- Chrome
- Edge
- Firefox
- Brave
- Opera
- Whale
- Yandex

### Operating Systems

- Windows
- macOS
- Linux

### Supported Content

- DreamCamVR live public VR streams
- DreamCamVR recorded VR videos
- HLS stream variants
- VR metadata (stereo packing, frame format, viewing angles)

### Not Supported

- Mobile browsers
- Safari
- Private, hidden, or inaccessible shows
- Bulk or multi-stream capture

## Privacy and Permissions

Supported regions: Worldwide.

Limitations:
- The performer must be publicly live for VR live capture to work.
- Private and hidden shows are not supported.
- Mobile and Safari browsers are not supported.
- One capture or download at a time for stable VR MP4 assembly.
- Available quality depends on what the source VR stream exposes.
- VR files are significantly larger than standard video and require adequate disk space.
- Internet connection is required during capture and download processing.
- You must already have access to the content.
- Email OTP sign-in is required to activate the free trial.

Permissions:
- downloads: Writes completed VR MP4 files to your device and keeps the download manager in sync.
- storage: Stores activation state, trial usage, and quality preferences locally between sessions.
- activeTab: Detects the current DreamCamVR page and injects player-level controls.
- tabs: Maintains capture state when you switch tabs during VR recording or download.
- scripting: Reads VR player data, stream metadata, and HLS variants from DreamCamVR pages.
- notifications: Shows alerts for completion and errors without requiring the popup to stay open.

## FAQ

### How do I record a live stream from DreamCamVR?

Go to a public live DreamCamVR performer page, wait for the player to initialize, then use the in-player button, extension popup, or the right-click menu to pick your quality and start the VR recording. The extension captures the HLS stream and converts it to a VR-ready MP4 when you stop.

### Can it download VR recordings too?

Yes. On supported VR recording pages, the extension switches to a standard download flow, identifies the available formats, and saves the selected one as an MP4.

### What quality options are available?

The extension reads the HLS master manifest and related DreamCam APIs to list the renditions available for the current VR stream or recording, which may include multiple resolutions up to 1080p or higher depending on the source.

### Does it preserve VR metadata?

Yes. When DreamCamVR provides stereo packing, frame format, or viewing-angle metadata, the extension carries that information over to the saved file so compatible VR headsets use the correct settings automatically.

### What format are the downloads?

All saved media is output as MP4. Direct file sources download immediately, while HLS-based sources are stitched into MP4 locally before the file is written.

### Where are files saved?

Completed downloads save through your browser''s normal Downloads workflow, with the extension handling the capture and assembly locally.

### Does it work for private shows?

No. The extension is designed for content your current session already has access to in a public or otherwise available setting. It does not bypass private-show paywalls, hidden-room restrictions, or account-gated content.

### Can I run multiple captures at once?

No. This tool is built for one active capture or download at a time so live polling, VR-aware segment stitching, and MP4 assembly remain stable.

### Which browsers are supported?

Desktop builds support Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Brave, Opera, Whale, and Yandex on Windows, macOS, and Linux. Safari and mobile browsers are not supported.

### How does the free trial work?

After completing the secure email OTP sign-in, you receive 3 free downloads on the current device. Unlimited access requires the monthly subscription.

### Why is no stream showing up?

Verify that the performer is publicly live and let the player finish initializing before checking the quality list. If the performer is offline, the room is private, or playback has not started, no stream will appear.

### Is my data private?

Yes. Stream detection, capture, and MP4 generation happen locally in your browser. Remote requests are limited to activation, update checks, and the original page or API calls needed to resolve the media you already access.

