EroMe provides no download button, and the albums you enjoy today can be deleted at any time. When a creator removes their content or the platform takes it down, those videos and images are gone permanently. EroMe Downloader provides a fast, dependable way to save entire albums to your device while they are still available.

Play a video on EroMe, click the download button that appears on the player, and choose your preferred quality. The extension also supports saving images from album pages. Files are stored as standard MP4 files for video and in their original format for images. HLS streams are automatically converted to MP4 right in the browser.

Completed files are organized into an EroMe folder on your device. Everything processes locally with no external servers involved. Start with 3 free downloads and upgrade for unlimited saves.

## Why It Exists

- Save EroMe albums before creators delete their content or the platform removes it.
- Download both videos and images from album pages in a single workflow.
- Convert HLS streams to MP4 locally in the browser for universal playback.
- Keep downloads private with entirely local processing and automatic file organization.

## Key Features

- Downloads videos and images from EroMe album and media pages
- In-page download button on the EroMe player for one-click video saves
- Album-aware detection that finds all media on the current page
- Quality selector showing available variants sorted by resolution
- HLS-to-MP4 conversion handled entirely in the browser
- Image extraction saving files in their original exposed format
- Built-in download manager with progress, speed, and cancel controls
- Auto-saves into an EroMe subfolder inside Downloads
- Right-click context menu for quick download starts
- Cross-browser support for Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Brave, Opera, Whale, and Yandex

## How It Works

- Install the extension: Add EroMe Downloader to your browser and verify your email via secure OTP.
- Open an EroMe album or media page: Navigate to the content you want to save.
- Click download: Use the in-page action, extension popup, or context menu to access download options.
- Choose quality and save: Pick your preferred resolution for videos, and the extension handles the rest.

## Reviews

- Saved my entire collection (5/5): Albums I bookmarked last month are already gone. Glad I downloaded them first with this tool. - Kenji Yamamoto
- Images and videos in one pass (4.9/5): Other tools only handle video. This one grabs the full album including images. - Lucia Fernandez
- Completely local (4.8/5): Nothing leaves my browser. The conversion process is smooth and the files are well organized. - Derek Wells

## Platform Support

### Browsers

- Chrome
- Edge
- Firefox
- Brave
- Opera
- Whale
- Yandex

### Operating Systems

- Windows
- macOS
- Linux

### Supported Content

- EroMe.com album and media pages
- Direct MP4 video sources
- HLS video streams
- Images from album pages

### Not Supported

- Mobile browsers
- Safari
- Live streams
- DRM-protected content

## Privacy and Permissions

Supported regions: Worldwide.

Limitations:
- You must press play before the extension can detect video sources.
- Live streams are not supported.
- Safari and mobile browsers are not supported.
- Available quality depends on what EroMe exposes for that content.
- The extension does not bypass DRM, account restrictions, or paywalls.
- Email OTP sign-in is required for the free trial.

Permissions:
- downloads: Saves media files to your device and tracks download manager progress.
- storage: Stores activation state, trial counters, and preferences locally.
- activeTab: Detects the current EroMe page and injects download controls.
- tabs: Keeps progress visible when switching between tabs.
- scripting: Reads media sources and injects page controls on supported tabs.
- notifications: Shows completion and error alerts.
- declarativeNetRequest: Applies request-header rules on matching media requests for consistent source fetching.

## FAQ

### How do I download an EroMe video?

Navigate to an EroMe album or media page, start playing the video, then use the in-page action, extension popup, or context menu to select your quality and download. The finished video gets saved as an MP4 file.

### Can I download images from EroMe albums too?

Yes. EroMe Downloader handles image extraction on album pages and saves image files in their original exposed format alongside any video downloads.

### What quality options are available for videos?

The extension presents available variants discovered from page and stream sources. Options are sorted by quality, with direct MP4 prioritized over HLS when both are available.

### What format are videos saved in?

Videos are stored as standard MP4 files. Direct MP4 sources save as-is, while HLS sources are stitched and converted to MP4 inside the browser.

### Does this support live streams?

No. This tool is designed for EroMe album and media-page downloads, not live-stream capture.

### Can I bulk-download entire albums automatically?

The extension is album-aware and detects all media on the current page, but the workflow focuses on explicit user-initiated downloads rather than fully automated bulk extraction.

### Why does the extension need scripting and offscreen permissions?

Scripting extracts media sources and injects page controls on supported tabs. Offscreen processing handles HLS-to-MP4 conversion locally.

### What is declarativeNetRequest used for?

It applies lightweight request-header rules on matching media requests to keep source fetching consistent across EroMe''s CDN infrastructure.

### Which browsers are supported?

Desktop builds support Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Brave, Opera, Whale, and Yandex on Windows, macOS, and Linux. Safari and mobile browsers are not supported.

### Is there a free trial?

Yes. You get 3 free trial downloads after email OTP verification. After that, the product uses a paid subscription for unlimited downloads.

### Is my data private?

Yes. Media detection, extraction, and conversion run locally in your browser. Authentication uses secure OTP, and media files are not uploaded to external servers.

