Fansly live streams are designed to be temporary. Once a broadcast ends, the content usually disappears unless the creator explicitly saves a replay. If you missed the window or your connection dropped mid-stream, that content is gone. Fansly Live Downloader captures authorized live broadcasts in real time and saves them as MP4 files directly to your device.

The extension works within your existing Fansly subscription. When a creator you follow goes live, open their page, start the recording, and the extension writes the incoming stream to an MP4 file as it arrives. If the stream drops, the captured data up to that point is preserved. When the broadcast finishes or you stop the recording, the completed file is ready for offline playback.

Everything processes locally on your machine. No copies are uploaded anywhere, no cloud storage is involved, and the recording quality matches whatever the broadcaster delivers to your browser.

## Why It Exists

- Record authorized Fansly live streams in real time before they end and disappear.
- Save broadcasts at the same quality your browser receives from Fansly.
- Keep recordings stored locally with no cloud uploads or external server involvement.
- Handle connection drops gracefully by preserving everything captured up to that point.

## Key Features

- Real-time live stream recording from authorized Fansly broadcasts
- Records at the stream quality delivered to your browser by Fansly
- Partial file preservation if the stream drops or gets interrupted
- Completed recordings saved as standard MP4 files
- Local-only processing with no cloud uploads or external storage
- Works with your existing Fansly subscription and session
- Built-in progress tracking during active recordings
- Auto-saves into your browser''s Downloads directory
- Cross-browser support for desktop Chromium and Firefox browsers
- Secure email OTP activation with free trial downloads included

## How It Works

- Install and activate: Add Fansly Live Downloader to your browser and sign in with the email OTP.
- Open a live Fansly broadcast: Visit the live page of a creator you are subscribed to.
- Start recording: Use the extension controls to begin capturing the live stream.
- Stop and save: End the recording when you are done and the MP4 file is saved to your Downloads folder.

## Reviews

- Never miss a live again (5/5): The real-time recording works flawlessly. I catch every broadcast I paid for even when my schedule does not align. - Rachel Torres
- Handles drops gracefully (4.9/5): My connection dropped mid-stream and the partial file was still perfectly playable. - Devon Chang
- Truly private (4.8/5): Everything stays on my machine. No cloud, no uploads, no traces anywhere else. - Kai Nakamura

## Platform Support

### Browsers

- Chrome
- Edge
- Firefox
- Brave
- Opera
- Whale
- Yandex

### Operating Systems

- Windows
- macOS
- Linux

### Supported Content

- Fansly live broadcasts you are subscribed to
- Real-time stream capture
- MP4 output files

### Not Supported

- Mobile browsers
- Safari
- Streams you do not have subscription access to
- Retroactive recording of ended broadcasts

## Privacy and Permissions

Supported regions: Worldwide.

Limitations:
- You must have an active Fansly subscription to the creator whose stream you want to record.
- The broadcast must be live; ended streams cannot be recorded retroactively.
- Recording quality matches what Fansly delivers to your browser.
- Safari and mobile browsers are not supported.
- Email OTP sign-in is required to activate the trial.

Permissions:
- downloads: Writes the recorded MP4 file to your device.
- storage: Stores activation state and recording preferences locally.
- activeTab: Detects the current Fansly page and manages recording controls.
- tabs: Maintains recording state when you switch between tabs.
- scripting: Reads stream data from the Fansly page to enable capture.
- notifications: Alerts you when recording completes or encounters an issue.

## FAQ

### Do I need a Fansly subscription to use this?

Yes. The extension records live streams you already have access to through your active Fansly subscription. It does not bypass paywalls, account restrictions, or content you have not paid for.

### What happens if the stream drops during recording?

The extension preserves all data captured up to the disconnection point. The partial file is playable. If the stream comes back, you can begin a new recording session.

### Can I record multiple streams at the same time?

Each browser tab handles one recording session. You can open multiple tabs with different streams, but performance depends on your system resources and connection speed.

### Does it capture chat or on-screen overlays?

No. The extension records the raw video and audio feed from the broadcast. Chat messages, tip notifications, and browser-side overlays are not included in the saved file.

### Are recordings stored anywhere besides my computer?

No. Files go directly to your local downloads folder. No copies are uploaded to cloud storage, and no recording data is sent to external servers.

### What video quality will the recording be?

The recording matches the stream quality that Fansly delivers to your browser. If the broadcaster streams in 1080p and your connection supports it, the recording will be at that same resolution.

