ThisVid is a community platform where users upload their own content. Videos can vanish at any moment when uploaders delete them or accounts get removed. ThisVid Downloader saves content to your device permanently.

Open a video on ThisVid, pick your quality, and download it as a clean MP4. The extension parses the ThisVid video player to identify all available stream sources. Batch queuing lets you add multiple URLs and process them sequentially. Automatic retry handles server-side issues without manual intervention.

Files save to a configurable output folder with support for custom naming rules and date-based subfolders. Everything runs locally in your browser with no external servers involved.

## Why It Exists

- Save user-uploaded ThisVid content before it gets deleted.
- Download with batch queuing for multiple videos.
- Automatic retry for handling server load spikes.
- Process everything locally and privately.

## Key Features

- ThisVid player parsing for source detection
- Batch URL queuing with sequential processing
- Automatic retry with server-issue detection
- Quality selection from available sources
- MP4 output without transcoding
- Configurable output folder with custom naming
- Date-based subfolder organization
- Local-only processing

## How It Works

- Install: Add ThisVid Downloader to your browser.
- Open a video: Navigate to a ThisVid video page.
- Download: Pick quality and save, or queue multiple URLs.
- Files save: To your configured output folder.

## Reviews

- Content preserved (5/5): Videos I saved last week are already gone from the site. - Marcus Bell
- Batch queue is great (4.9/5): Queue up multiple URLs and let them process. - Nina Schultz
- Reliable retry (4.8/5): Server issues get handled automatically. No babysitting needed. - Raj Patel

